# Project rules

This repository is a GPUI-based Markdown editor, not the Zed IDE.

## Boundaries

- Do not reintroduce Zed IDE crates such as `project`, `workspace`, `editor`, `language`, or `multi_buffer` into the product path.
- Keep the product runtime centered on `markdown_editor`, `md_editor`, `md_buffer`, `md_text`, `md_rope`, `md_sum_tree`, `md_theme`, `md_settings`, `md_assets`, `markdown_wysiwyg`, and `gpui`.
- `gpui` is consumed as a Cargo dependency. Do not vendor GPUI source into this repository.

## Licensing

- Treat `md_rope`, `md_text`, and `md_editor` as GPL-3.0-or-later Zed-derived code.
- Treat `md_sum_tree`, `collections`, `util_macros`, and `tooling/perf` as Apache-2.0 Zed-derived components.
- Keep `NOTICE`, `LICENSE`, `LICENSE-APACHE`, and per-crate license metadata aligned when moving code between crates.

## Development

- Use `rg` for searching.
- Use `cargo check -p markdown_editor` for the primary build check.
- Use `cargo test -p md_sum_tree`, `cargo test -p md_rope`, and `cargo test -p md_text` for the core text stack.
- Use `cargo perf-test -p md_editor` only when intentionally running perf triage.

## Editing

- Prefer small, local changes that preserve the current `md_*` crate boundaries.
- Do not remove attribution or license notices when simplifying Zed-derived code.
- Do not add Zed branding, Zed fonts, or Zed product names to user-facing defaults.
